<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ product }} model-update comparison — {{ c.side_a.display_name }} → {{ c.side_b.display_name }}</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink:#14181f; --muted:#5a6577; --rule:#d5dce4; --panel:#f5f7fa;
          --same:#1b7a44; --chg:#b8471f; --na:#5a6577; }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin:0; font: 15px/1.7 system-ui, sans-serif; color:var(--ink); }
  .wrap { max-width: 62rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 0 0 .25rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink);
       padding-bottom:.3rem; margin: 2.2rem 0 .8rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .92em; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .45rem .6rem;
           border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
  th { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  .num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; text-align: right; }
  .v { font-weight: 700; font-size: .85em; letter-spacing: .03em; }
  .v.CHANGED { color: var(--chg); }
  .v.NOT_SEPARATED { color: var(--same); }
  .v.INSUFFICIENT { color: var(--na); }
  .st { font-size:.8em; font-weight:600; }
  .st.PASS { color: var(--same); } .st.FAIL { color: var(--chg); }
  .st.WARN { color:#a06a00; } .st.INSUFFICIENT, .st.NOT_TESTED { color: var(--na); }
  .box { background: var(--panel); border-left: 4px solid var(--ink);
         padding: .8rem 1rem; margin: 1rem 0; }
  ul { margin:.3rem 0 .6rem 1.2rem; padding:0; }
  footer { margin-top:3rem; border-top:1px solid var(--rule);
           padding-top:1rem; font-size:.85em; color:var(--muted); }
  code { background: var(--panel); padding:0 .3em; border-radius:3px;
         font-size:.9em; }
</style>
</head>
<body><div class="wrap">

<h1>Model-update comparison</h1>
<div class="muted">{{ product }} · suite {{ c.suite_id }}@{{ c.suite_version }}
· claim {{ c.claim_id }} · compare <code>{{ c.compare_hash[:16] }}…</code></div>

<div class="box">
  <b>A (baseline):</b> {{ c.side_a.display_name }}
  <span class="muted">v{{ c.side_a.model_version }} ·
  {{ c.side_a.n_windows }} windows · bundle
  <code>{{ c.side_a.bundle_hash[:12] }}…</code></span><br>
  <b>B (candidate):</b> {{ c.side_b.display_name }}
  <span class="muted">v{{ c.side_b.model_version }} ·
  {{ c.side_b.n_windows }} windows · bundle
  <code>{{ c.side_b.bundle_hash[:12] }}…</code></span>
</div>

<p>Per metric, this report answers one question: <em>did the update change
this dimension's window distribution?</em> (permutation test over windows,
{{ c.inference.multiple_testing }}-adjusted, line α =
{{ c.inference.alpha }}). Each row also shows what both versions do against
the empirical reference, so a detected change can be read as toward or away
from realism. Verdicts do not aggregate.</p>

<h2>Per-metric verdicts</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Verdict (A→B)</th><th class="num">KS(A,B)</th>
      <th class="num">p (adj)</th><th class="num">median A</th>
      <th class="num">median B</th><th>A vs ref</th><th>B vs ref</th></tr>
  {% for r in c.results %}
  {% set mid = r.metric_ref.split("@")[0] %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ mid }}</code></td>
    <td><span class="v {{ r.verdict }}">{{ r.verdict }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(r.ks_ab) if r.ks_ab is not none else "—" }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.4f"|format(r.adjusted_p_value) if r.adjusted_p_value is not none else "—" }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.4g"|format(r.median_a) if r.median_a is not none else "—" }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.4g"|format(r.median_b) if r.median_b is not none else "—" }}</td>
    <td><span class="st {{ r.status_a_vs_reference.value }}">{{ r.status_a_vs_reference.value }}</span></td>
    <td><span class="st {{ r.status_b_vs_reference.value }}">{{ r.status_b_vs_reference.value }}</span></td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>How to read this</h2>
<ul>
  <li><b>CHANGED</b> — the update moved this metric's window distribution
      beyond the calibrated line. Whether that is acceptable is a claim
      decision, not a statistic: check the vs-reference columns.</li>
  <li><b>NOT_SEPARATED</b> — no detectable difference at this line with this
      many windows. Not a claim of equality.</li>
  <li><b>INSUFFICIENT</b> — fewer than 5 usable windows on a side.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Caveats</h2>
<ul>{% for cv in c.caveats %}<li>{{ cv }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

<h2>Provenance</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Compare</th><td><code>{{ c.compare_id }}</code> ·
      {{ product|lower }} {{ c.sieve_version }} · seed {{ c.master_seed }}</td></tr>
  <tr><th>Suite hash</th><td><code>{{ c.suite_hash[:16] }}…</code></td></tr>
  <tr><th>Inputs</th><td>A input sha256 <code>{{ c.side_a.input_hash[:12] }}…</code>
      · B input sha256 <code>{{ c.side_b.input_hash[:12] }}…</code>
      (both runs verified before comparison)</td></tr>
</table>

<footer>{{ footer }}<br>
Verify: <code>sha256sum -c compare.sha256</code> · both source runs:
<code>sieve verify &lt;run-dir&gt;</code></footer>
</div></body>
</html>
